    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d244">

                <pb facs="0443" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1180.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Cairo</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-07T19:00:00+02:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1914, 10 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11:58 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>General commanding British Egypt issued to-day proclamation in the name of King
                    George assuming sole burden of defending Egypt against Turkey, claiming
                    violation Egyptian frontier and agreeing not to ask Mohammedan Egyptians’
                    assistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Arnold</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
